<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!-- cairo 1.0, as GObject introspection describes it (the records and
     their cairo-gobject GTypes, and the enums, their values read from cairo.h
     by the compiler), and what upstream's cairo-1.0.gir leaves out: the
     drawing API as methods, `cr.rectangle(...)`, which GJS writes by hand.
     The binder carries it for systems that ship no cairo-1.0.gir, and
     prefers it where one is shipped, since that one has no methods. Every
     declaration here is compiled against cairo.h by the binder's self-check,
     so a wrong one is dropped, not believed. Written by a script from a table
     of methods and the header's enums; regenerate rather than edit. -->
